  - computational number theory
abstract: >-
  Seven additional indices n for which the Lucas number L(n) is a Smith number:
  1692, 1770, 1798, 1865, 1899, 2331 and 7474. Complete prime factorizations
  were reconstructed from published tables and verified with independent
  primality tests. The largest term, L(7474), has 1562 decimal digits.
